WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:03.979
Here's a quick story, just about another one
of these self-inflicted embarrassments for

00:00:03.979 --> 00:00:05.169
the current administration.

00:00:05.169 --> 00:00:10.360
Yesterday, you actually had two press events,
but both of which I covered live in the morning.

00:00:10.360 --> 00:00:14.799
You had Donald Trump's press secretary, Kaley
McKenny, do a standard press briefing where

00:00:14.799 --> 00:00:17.750
she comes out, speaks for like 90 seconds.

00:00:17.750 --> 00:00:19.970
75 seconds are usually her lies.

00:00:19.970 --> 00:00:21.520
The other 15 are just saying hello.

00:00:21.520 --> 00:00:25.680
And then in the afternoon, Donald Trump did
his own press briefing.

00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:29.990
And what was very interesting was that in
the morning, the topic of testing came up

00:00:29.990 --> 00:00:33.500
and the topic of Trump not wearing a mask
came up.

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:38.480
And weirdly, when Kaley McCannon, he was trying
to defend Trump, not wearing a mask in many

00:00:38.480 --> 00:00:39.480
situations.

00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:45.800
She said, listen, Trump's tested multiple
times a day for Corona virus, which is weird.

00:00:45.800 --> 00:00:51.539
And I'll play that part of this for you first.

00:00:51.539 --> 00:00:52.539
And don't tell me he hasn't won.

00:00:52.539 --> 00:00:53.539
So it's sending mixed signals.

00:00:53.539 --> 00:00:54.679
The president wore a mask in May.

00:00:54.679 --> 00:00:57.620
The president wore a mask at Walter Reed out
of an abundance of caution.

00:00:57.620 --> 00:01:01.809
But as I've made clear from this podium, the
president is the most tested man in America.

00:01:01.809 --> 00:01:04.580
He's tested more than anyone multiple times
a day.

00:01:04.580 --> 00:01:07.460
And we believe that he's acting appropriately.

00:01:07.460 --> 00:01:13.000
The president is tested for corona virus multiple
times per day.

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:16.090
That's definitely odd, but OK.

00:01:16.090 --> 00:01:18.570
So then hours later, you knew it was going
to happen.

00:01:18.570 --> 00:01:22.920
Donald Trump was asked earlier, your press
secretary said you're tested multiple times

00:01:22.920 --> 00:01:24.950
per day for Corona virus.

00:01:24.950 --> 00:01:27.040
Can you talk about how frequently that's happening?

00:01:27.040 --> 00:01:32.050
And Trump says he looks clearly confused and
he says, I can't even think of one time where

00:01:32.050 --> 00:01:34.820
I was tested more than once in a day.

00:01:34.820 --> 00:01:37.250
Usually I'm tested once every two or three
days.

00:01:37.250 --> 00:01:38.250
What was.

00:01:38.250 --> 00:01:39.840
Yeah, take a look to president.

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:41.790
First, though, Chorney clarification.

00:01:41.790 --> 00:01:46.210
Your press secretary said today that you sometimes
take more than one test today.

00:01:46.210 --> 00:01:47.210
Why is that?

00:01:47.210 --> 00:01:48.210
How?

00:01:48.210 --> 00:01:49.400
Well, I didn't know about more than one.

00:01:49.400 --> 00:01:53.930
I do test probably on average a test every
two days, three days.

00:01:53.930 --> 00:01:58.760
And I don't know of any time I've taken two
tests in one day, but I could see that happening.

00:01:58.760 --> 00:02:02.830
So this is once again not an issue of interpretation.

00:02:02.830 --> 00:02:07.880
This is just a very concrete, practical matter.

00:02:07.880 --> 00:02:13.730
Kaley McKenny defends Trump's lack of mask
wearing by saying he's getting tested multiple

00:02:13.730 --> 00:02:14.870
times per day.

00:02:14.870 --> 00:02:20.830
Now, if that were true, that would raise questions
of why are most people waiting five to seven

00:02:20.830 --> 00:02:22.439
days for results?

00:02:22.439 --> 00:02:25.319
And Trump's getting multiple tests with almost
immediate results.

00:02:25.319 --> 00:02:27.319
Although I get it, he's the president.

00:02:27.319 --> 00:02:31.159
But the point is, we still have a testing
problem in this country.

00:02:31.159 --> 00:02:35.269
If you don't get your results back for five
to seven days, as many people don't.

00:02:35.269 --> 00:02:39.870
You can spread the disease to multiple people
while you're waiting for your test results.

00:02:39.870 --> 00:02:43.900
And Trump is barely wearing a mask and getting
multiple tests per day.

00:02:43.900 --> 00:02:48.879
But then Trump just straight up says, I don't
know anything about multiple tests in a day.

00:02:48.879 --> 00:02:51.459
I'm tested once every two to three days.

00:02:51.459 --> 00:02:55.560
So if there is a briefing today, I'm sure
Kaylie McEnany will be asked about it.

00:02:55.560 --> 00:03:00.110
I'm sure she'll have some prepared explanation
that may already have happened by the time

00:03:00.110 --> 00:03:03.219
you see this, or maybe there will be no press
briefing at all today.

00:03:03.219 --> 00:03:06.650
But as usual, caught lying again.

00:03:06.650 --> 00:03:10.939
And the theme is they go too far when there's
bye.

00:03:10.939 --> 00:03:14.500
I don't want to say this is this is a normal
question.

00:03:14.500 --> 00:03:15.769
Everybody's told to wear masks.

00:03:15.769 --> 00:03:20.829
Why isn't Trump wearing one when they see
a hostile question and accusatory question?

00:03:20.829 --> 00:03:26.139
As far as they're concerned, they go overboard
in trying to defend.

00:03:26.139 --> 00:03:27.419
And that's how you get this.

00:03:27.419 --> 00:03:28.680
Why isn't Trump wearing a mask?

00:03:28.680 --> 00:03:29.939
Oh, he's tested all the time.

00:03:29.939 --> 00:03:31.730
He's tested multiple times a day.

00:03:31.730 --> 00:03:33.599
And there's other examples of this.

00:03:33.599 --> 00:03:37.900
When Trump says something racially off color
and then he's called on it.

00:03:37.900 --> 00:03:41.200
He'll say things like, I am the least racist
person ever.

00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:42.450
That got a hold on a sec.

00:03:42.450 --> 00:03:44.299
That's a weird thing to say.

00:03:44.299 --> 00:03:48.959
Maybe just say you're not racist, but the
least racist person ever, you know, saying

00:03:48.959 --> 00:03:49.959
I'm not racist.

00:03:49.959 --> 00:03:51.859
That wouldn't be any more believable, quite
frankly.

00:03:51.859 --> 00:03:54.170
But it would at least be more plausible.

00:03:54.170 --> 00:03:59.349
Or when asked about testing, Trump says we
have the best and the most testing.

00:03:59.349 --> 00:04:00.349
Well, no way.

00:04:00.349 --> 00:04:01.349
The best.

00:04:01.349 --> 00:04:02.650
Not really the most.

00:04:02.650 --> 00:04:03.650
No.

00:04:03.650 --> 00:04:05.019
Not per capita.

00:04:05.019 --> 00:04:06.340
The fastest results.

00:04:06.340 --> 00:04:07.579
Certainly not.

00:04:07.579 --> 00:04:11.769
When asked about deaths, Trump says we have
the lowest mortality rate.

00:04:11.769 --> 00:04:12.769
Well, no, we don't.

00:04:12.769 --> 00:04:15.030
Of course, none of these things are true.

00:04:15.030 --> 00:04:20.859
And it is another one of these little self-inflicted
cuts that comes from trying to be hyperbolic

00:04:20.859 --> 00:04:22.919
and go against anything perceived.

00:04:22.919 --> 00:04:30.360
I mean, there's so trigonal, there's so thin
skinned that would qualify as just a basic,

00:04:30.360 --> 00:04:35.949
obvious journalistic question in any other
country with a free press here, these are

00:04:35.949 --> 00:04:37.060
seen as attacks.

00:04:37.060 --> 00:06:05.050
And they actually generate obvious and provable
lies.

